//@version=6
// =============================================================================
// Time-of-Day RVOL Regime Filter v1.0 (5T Pine Suite · Desk Kit)
//
// WHAT THIS IS.
// The suite's documented selection edge is relative volume (Zarattini /
// Barbon / Aziz 2024 — expectancy scaled with RVOL; the edge concentrated
// in Stocks in Play). This filter measures the JOINT condition on THIS
// chart: exact time-of-day RVOL elevation × regime — and counts whether
// elevated-RVOL bars in each directional regime showed next-bar follow-
// through (continuation in the regime's direction), Wilson-bounded, AGAINST
// that same regime's non-elevated baseline. The DELTA is the point: does
// elevation tilt follow-through beyond the regime's base rate here, or not?
// Intraday only — the time-of-day machinery is meaningless on dailies and
// the HUD says so instead of pretending.
//
// RESEARCH BASIS, stated plainly.
// Zarattini/Barbon/Aziz (2024): ORB expectancy scaled with relative volume;
// negative below ~1x, concentrated in the high-RVOL tail. RVOL is a
// SELECTION statistic, not an entry signal — suite doctrine. Session volume
// follows a U-shape (0935–1530 framing): the first 30–60 minutes dominate,
// so elevation is easiest and noisiest at the open — the HUD carries that
// warning permanently. Exact time-of-day RVOL machinery is copied from the
// SIP RVOL Screener v1.1 (KLQuant matrix method): cum volume vs the average
// cum volume at this same bar-of-day over the prior N days, confirmed
// writes, current day excluded from its own average, warm after 5 prior days.
//
// HONESTY, stated plainly.
//   1. Follow-through is counted history on this chart — next-bar
//      continuation, nothing longer, nothing predictive.
//   2. The tilt verdict (Wilson lower bound of the elevated rate above the
//      baseline rate by a margin, with a minimum n) is a labeled heuristic.
//   3. Day-boundary bars are excluded from counting — overnight gaps would
//      contaminate a "next-bar" measurement.
//
// Non-repaint: matrix writes, counters, and all statistics advance on
// confirmed bars only; the live bar's RVOL updates intrabar as cum volume
// grows (that is the nature of the statistic) and settles at the close.
// Alerts fire on confirmed bars. Decision support only — a human places
// every trade. Risk controls outrank all signals.
//
// v1.0 changelog (2026-07-17):
//   Initial release. Exact time-of-day RVOL (SIP v1.1 matrix machinery:
//   days×bars matrix, confirmed writes, current-day exclusion, warm gate
//   5 prior days); elevation threshold (default 1.5x per the research
//   floor); per-regime next-bar continuation counts, elevated vs baseline,
//   with Wilson lower bounds and thin flags; tilt verdict per side
//   (labeled heuristic: Wlo(elev) > base + 2pts with n>=30); regime source
//   = external link (strict -1/0/+1 validation) with internal hard-
//   threshold z fallback, HUD names the live source; intraday-only guard
//   (Noise-Area pattern); RVOL plot + threshold line + elevated tint;
//   session U-shape warning row; tiered HUD; Data-Window exports;
//   elevated-in-directional-regime alert with optional JSON payloads
//   (default OFF). Behavior-adjacent options ship at conservative
//   defaults. Evidence label: needs user run.
// =============================================================================
indicator("Time-of-Day RVOL Regime Filter v1.0", shorttitle = "TOD RVOL v1",
     overlay = false)

grp_mode = "0 · Mode"
grp_rv   = "1 · Time-of-Day RVOL"
grp_link = "2 · Regime Source"
grp_meas = "3 · Follow-Through Measurement"
grp_dsp  = "4 · Display"

variant_tag = input.string("v1.0-base", "Variant tag (freeze-the-config discipline)", group = grp_mode,
     tooltip = "Label this exact settings set. Any settings change = new tag = new variant with its own validation cycle. The tag prints on the HUD and in alerts so screenshots self-document.")

rvol_days = input.int(20, "RVOL lookback (days)", minval = 3, maxval = 60, group = grp_rv,
     tooltip = "How many prior days feed the same-time-of-day average. Matches the SIP screener convention.")
tod_max_bars = input.int(400, "Max bars per day stored", minval = 50, maxval = 500, group = grp_rv,
     tooltip = "390 one-minute RTH bars; 400 covers padding. Lower on higher intraday timeframes is fine.")
elev_thr = input.float(1.5, "Elevated at RVOL >=", minval = 0.5, maxval = 30.0, step = 0.1, group = grp_rv,
     tooltip = "Research floor, not a target: expectancy was negative below ~1x and scaled with RVOL — the fat tail (3x+) is where the edge concentrated. Elevation selects; it never signals.")

use_regime_link = input.bool(false, "Use external regime link", group = grp_link)
regime_src = input.source(close, "Regime link (wire to a REGIME_EXPORT)", group = grp_link,
     tooltip = "Wire to any suite script's REGIME_EXPORT. Validated STRICTLY: only exact -1 / 0 / +1 values count. Anything else falls back to the internal classifier and the HUD flags LINK?.")
z_lookback = input.int(20, "Internal fallback: z lookback (bars)", minval = 5, maxval = 250, group = grp_link,
     tooltip = "The fallback classifier is the suite observation — volatility-normalized window return z-score — with hard thresholds and no hysteresis. A convenience stand-in, not a substitute for the flagship engine.")
z_enter = input.float(0.85, "Internal fallback: z threshold", minval = 0.10, maxval = 3.00, step = 0.05, group = grp_link)

min_side_n = input.int(30, "Thin-sample warning (elevated n)", minval = 5, maxval = 1000, group = grp_meas,
     tooltip = "Below this many elevated samples on a side, the row carries the suite's thin-sample flag and the tilt verdict reads 'thin'. Wilson lower bounds do the honesty work either way.")
tilt_margin = input.float(2.0, "Tilt verdict margin (pts)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 20.0, step = 0.5, group = grp_meas,
     tooltip = "Verdict 'tilts' requires Wlo(elevated continuation) to exceed the baseline continuation rate by this many percentage points, with the minimum n met. A labeled heuristic, not a significance test.")

hud_mode = input.string("Full", "HUD mode", options = ["Off", "Micro", "Full"], group = grp_dsp)
hud_pos_in = input.string("top_right", "HUD position", options = ["top_left", "top_center", "top_right", "bottom_left", "bottom_center", "bottom_right"], group = grp_dsp)
show_rvol_plot = input.bool(true, "Plot time-of-day RVOL", group = grp_dsp)
show_elev_tint = input.bool(true, "Elevated background tint", group = grp_dsp)
use_json_alerts = input.bool(false, "JSON alert payloads (webhook)", group = grp_dsp,
     tooltip = "OFF: human-readable alert text. ON: machine-readable JSON for webhook automation. Display-layer only.")

// =============================================================================
// Palette & helpers (suite standard)
// =============================================================================
c_bull  = color.rgb(89, 159, 125)
c_bear  = color.rgb(190, 96, 111)
c_neut  = color.rgb(112, 126, 148)
c_gold  = color.rgb(214, 162, 82)
c_panel = color.new(#0E1316, 5)
c_cell  = color.new(#151D22, 7)
c_cell2 = color.new(#10171B, 9)
c_frame = color.new(#5BD6B0, 88)
c_text  = color.white
c_dim   = color.new(color.white, 45)
c_faint = color.new(color.white, 68)

f_pos(_s) =>
    switch _s
        "top_left"      => position.top_left
        "top_center"    => position.top_center
        "top_right"     => position.top_right
        "bottom_left"   => position.bottom_left
        "bottom_center" => position.bottom_center
        "bottom_right"  => position.bottom_right
        => position.top_right
f_fmt(_x, _d) =>
    _m = math.pow(10.0, _d)
    na(_x) ? "n/a" : str.tostring(math.round(_x * _m) / _m)
f_tcell(_tbl, _c, _r, _txt, _col, _bg) =>
    table.cell(_tbl, _c, _r, _txt, text_color = _col, bgcolor = _bg, text_size = size.tiny, text_halign = text.align_center)
// Wilson score lower bound (z = 1.96), suite-standard honesty for counted rates.
f_wilson_lo(_p, _n) =>
    _n <= 0 or na(_p) ? float(na) :
         (_p + 1.96 * 1.96 / (2 * _n) - 1.96 * math.sqrt((_p * (1 - _p) + 1.96 * 1.96 / (4 * _n)) / _n)) / (1 + 1.96 * 1.96 / _n)
f_rname(_s) =>
    _s == 1 ? "Bull" : _s == -1 ? "Bear" : "Neutral"
f_rcol(_s) =>
    _s == 1 ? c_bull : _s == -1 ? c_bear : c_neut
f_new_day() =>
    ta.change(time("D")) != 0

// =============================================================================
// Regime source: external link (strict -1/0/+1) with internal z fallback.
// The HUD names whichever source is live; an enabled-but-invalid link reads
// LINK? and the internal classifier takes over rather than polluting counts.
// =============================================================================
one_bar_ret = not na(close[1]) and close > 0 and close[1] > 0 ? math.log(close / close[1]) : float(na)
win_ret = not na(close[z_lookback]) and close > 0 and close[z_lookback] > 0 ? math.log(close / close[z_lookback]) : float(na)
win_vol = ta.stdev(one_bar_ret, z_lookback) * math.sqrt(z_lookback)
obs_z = not na(win_ret) and not na(win_vol) and win_vol > 0 ? win_ret / win_vol : float(na)
int z_state = na(obs_z) ? 0 : obs_z > z_enter ? 1 : obs_z < -z_enter ? -1 : 0
_rvl = regime_src
link_valid = use_regime_link and not na(_rvl) and (_rvl == -1.0 or _rvl == 0.0 or _rvl == 1.0)
int regime_now = link_valid ? int(_rvl) : z_state
regime_ready = link_valid or not na(obs_z)
regime_src_txt = link_valid ? "external link" : use_regime_link ? "LINK? → internal z" : "internal z"

// =============================================================================
// Exact time-of-day RVOL (matrix machinery copied from SIP v1.1, per KLQuant):
// days×bars matrix of cum volume, confirmed writes, current day excluded from
// its own average. is_newday is hoisted to a single call site so the ta.change
// inside evaluates unconditionally every bar.
// =============================================================================
bool is_newday = f_new_day()
var matrix<float> tod_m = matrix.new<float>(60, 500, na)
var int tod_row = 0
var int day_b = -1
var float chart_cum = 0.0
day_b := is_newday ? 0 : day_b + 1
chart_cum := is_newday ? nz(volume) : chart_cum + nz(volume)
_days_eff = math.min(rvol_days, 60)
_bars_eff = math.min(tod_max_bars, 500)
if is_newday
    tod_row := (tod_row + 1) % _days_eff
    for c = 0 to _bars_eff - 1
        matrix.set(tod_m, tod_row, c, na)
if barstate.isconfirmed and day_b >= 0 and day_b < _bars_eff
    matrix.set(tod_m, tod_row, day_b, chart_cum)
float tod_sum = 0.0
int tod_n = 0
if day_b >= 0 and day_b < _bars_eff
    for r = 0 to _days_eff - 1
        if r != tod_row
            _v = matrix.get(tod_m, r, day_b)
            if not na(_v)
                tod_sum += _v
                tod_n += 1
rvol_tod = timeframe.isintraday and tod_n > 0 and tod_sum > 0 ? chart_cum / (tod_sum / tod_n) : float(na)
bool tod_warm = timeframe.isintraday and tod_n >= 5
bool elevated = tod_warm and not na(rvol_tod) and rvol_tod >= elev_thr

// =============================================================================
// Joint measurement (confirmed, warmed, intraday): condition read on the PRIOR
// confirmed bar, outcome = this bar's close vs close[1] in the regime's
// direction. First bar of a day never scores — overnight gaps would
// contaminate a next-bar measurement. Baseline = same regime, NOT elevated.
// =============================================================================
var int bull_e_n = 0
var int bull_e_h = 0
var int bull_b_n = 0
var int bull_b_h = 0
var int bear_e_n = 0
var int bear_e_h = 0
var int bear_b_n = 0
var int bear_b_h = 0
if barstate.isconfirmed and timeframe.isintraday and not is_newday and not na(close[1])
    int _r1 = regime_now[1]
    bool _w1 = tod_warm[1]
    float _rv1 = rvol_tod[1]
    if _w1 and not na(_rv1) and _r1 != 0
        bool _elev1 = _rv1 >= elev_thr
        bool _cont = _r1 == 1 ? close > close[1] : close < close[1]
        if _r1 == 1
            if _elev1
                bull_e_n += 1
                bull_e_h += _cont ? 1 : 0
            else
                bull_b_n += 1
                bull_b_h += _cont ? 1 : 0
        else
            if _elev1
                bear_e_n += 1
                bear_e_h += _cont ? 1 : 0
            else
                bear_b_n += 1
                bear_b_h += _cont ? 1 : 0

float bull_e_r = bull_e_n > 0 ? bull_e_h * 1.0 / bull_e_n : float(na)
float bull_b_r = bull_b_n > 0 ? bull_b_h * 1.0 / bull_b_n : float(na)
float bear_e_r = bear_e_n > 0 ? bear_e_h * 1.0 / bear_e_n : float(na)
float bear_b_r = bear_b_n > 0 ? bear_b_h * 1.0 / bear_b_n : float(na)
float bull_e_wlo = f_wilson_lo(bull_e_r, bull_e_n)
float bear_e_wlo = f_wilson_lo(bear_e_r, bear_e_n)
// Tilt verdict per side: +1 tilts / 0 no tilt / na thin (labeled heuristic)
float bull_tilt = bull_e_n < min_side_n or na(bull_b_r) or na(bull_e_wlo) ? float(na) :
     bull_e_wlo > bull_b_r + tilt_margin / 100.0 ? 1.0 : 0.0
float bear_tilt = bear_e_n < min_side_n or na(bear_b_r) or na(bear_e_wlo) ? float(na) :
     bear_e_wlo > bear_b_r + tilt_margin / 100.0 ? 1.0 : 0.0
f_tiltname(_t) =>
    na(_t) ? "thin" : _t == 1.0 ? "tilts" : "no tilt"

// =============================================================================
// Plots, tint, exports
// =============================================================================
plot(show_rvol_plot ? rvol_tod : na, "RVOL (time-of-day, exact)", color = elevated ? c_gold : color.new(c_neut, 25), linewidth = 2)
hline(1.0, "Parity", color = color.new(color.white, 88), linestyle = hline.style_dotted)
hline(elev_thr, "Elevated threshold", color = color.new(color.white, 80), linestyle = hline.style_dotted)
bgcolor(show_elev_tint and elevated ? color.new(c_gold, 85) : na, title = "Elevated tint")

plot(rvol_tod, "TRF_RVOL_TOD_EXPORT", color = color.new(color.white, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(elevated ? 1.0 : 0.0, "TRF_ELEVATED_EXPORT", color = color.new(color.white, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(bull_tilt, "TRF_BULL_TILT_EXPORT", color = color.new(color.white, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(bear_tilt, "TRF_BEAR_TILT_EXPORT", color = color.new(color.white, 100), display = display.data_window)
plot(tod_warm ? 1.0 : 0.0, "TRF_WARM_EXPORT", color = color.new(color.white, 100), display = display.data_window)

// =============================================================================
// HUD
// =============================================================================
var table hud = table.new(f_pos(hud_pos_in), 2, 8, bgcolor = c_panel, frame_color = c_frame,
     frame_width = 1, border_color = color.new(color.white, 92), border_width = 1)
if barstate.islast and hud_mode != "Off"
    _state_txt = not timeframe.isintraday ? "INTRADAY ONLY — load an intraday chart" :
         not tod_warm ? "WARMING · " + str.tostring(math.min(tod_n, 5)) + "/5 prior days" :
         elevated ? f_fmt(rvol_tod, 2) + "x · ELEVATED · " + f_rname(regime_now) : f_fmt(rvol_tod, 2) + "x · quiet"
    _state_bg = not timeframe.isintraday ? color.new(c_bear, 35) : not tod_warm ? c_cell :
         elevated ? color.new(c_gold, 55) : c_cell
    f_tcell(hud, 0, 0, "TOD RVOL " + variant_tag, c_text, c_frame)
    f_tcell(hud, 1, 0, _state_txt, c_text, _state_bg)
    if hud_mode == "Full" and timeframe.isintraday
        f_tcell(hud, 0, 1, "RVOL (tod, exact)", c_dim, c_panel)
        f_tcell(hud, 1, 1, f_fmt(rvol_tod, 2) + "x · thr " + f_fmt(elev_thr, 1) + "x · slot n" + str.tostring(tod_n) + (tod_warm ? "" : " · warming"), not tod_warm ? c_faint : elevated ? c_gold : c_dim, c_cell)
        f_tcell(hud, 0, 2, "Regime · source", c_dim, c_panel)
        f_tcell(hud, 1, 2, f_rname(regime_now) + " · " + regime_src_txt, use_regime_link and not link_valid ? c_bear : c_dim, c_cell)
        f_tcell(hud, 0, 3, "Bull: elev vs base", c_dim, c_panel)
        f_tcell(hud, 1, 3, "cont " + f_fmt(bull_e_r * 100.0, 0) + "% (Wlo " + f_fmt(bull_e_wlo * 100.0, 0) + ", n" + str.tostring(bull_e_n) + (bull_e_n < min_side_n ? " !" : "") + ") vs " + f_fmt(bull_b_r * 100.0, 0) + "% (n" + str.tostring(bull_b_n) + ")", bull_e_n < min_side_n ? c_faint : c_bull, c_cell)
        f_tcell(hud, 0, 4, "Bear: elev vs base", c_dim, c_panel)
        f_tcell(hud, 1, 4, "cont " + f_fmt(bear_e_r * 100.0, 0) + "% (Wlo " + f_fmt(bear_e_wlo * 100.0, 0) + ", n" + str.tostring(bear_e_n) + (bear_e_n < min_side_n ? " !" : "") + ") vs " + f_fmt(bear_b_r * 100.0, 0) + "% (n" + str.tostring(bear_b_n) + ")", bear_e_n < min_side_n ? c_faint : c_bear, c_cell)
        f_tcell(hud, 0, 5, "Tilt verdict (labeled heuristic)", c_dim, c_panel)
        f_tcell(hud, 1, 5, "Bull: " + f_tiltname(bull_tilt) + " · Bear: " + f_tiltname(bear_tilt), bull_tilt == 1.0 or bear_tilt == 1.0 ? c_gold : c_dim, c_cell)
        f_tcell(hud, 0, 6, "Session note", c_dim, c_panel)
        f_tcell(hud, 1, 6, "first 30–60 min dominate volume — elevation is easiest and noisiest at the open", c_faint, c_cell)
        f_tcell(hud, 0, 7, "*selection context on this chart", c_faint, c_panel)
        f_tcell(hud, 1, 7, "never a signal · not advice", c_faint, c_panel)

// =============================================================================
// Alerts (confirmed-bar onset of elevated-in-directional-regime)
// =============================================================================
bool hot_now = timeframe.isintraday and elevated and regime_now != 0
bool hot_new = hot_now and not hot_now[1]
alertcondition(hot_new and barstate.isconfirmed, "Elevated RVOL in directional regime (confirmed)", "TOD RVOL Filter: time-of-day RVOL elevated while the regime is directional — selection context only")
if barstate.isconfirmed and hot_new
    if use_json_alerts
        alert('{"ev":"tod_rvol","sym":"' + syminfo.ticker + '","tf":"' + timeframe.period + '","rvol":' + (na(rvol_tod) ? "null" : f_fmt(rvol_tod, 2)) + ',"regime":"' + f_rname(regime_now) + '","slot_n":' + str.tostring(tod_n) + ',"variant":"' + variant_tag + '","t":' + str.tostring(time) + '}', alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
    else
        alert("TOD RVOL [" + variant_tag + "]: " + syminfo.ticker + " elevated " + f_fmt(rvol_tod, 2) +
             "x (thr " + f_fmt(elev_thr, 1) + "x) in " + f_rname(regime_now) + " regime · selection context only", alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// =============================================================================
// End of file · Time-of-Day RVOL Regime Filter v1.0
